  "3DGS": { abstractEn: "3D Gaussian Splatting introduces anisotropic 3D Gaussians as a direct radiance field representation, avoiding the costly ray-marching required by NeRF. It employs a tile-based differentiable rasterization pipeline with GPU-friendly alpha-compositing for efficient novel view synthesis. Adaptive density control splits and prunes Gaussians during training to progressively refine scene geometry. The method achieves real-time rendering at over 100 FPS while matching or exceeding NeRF's visual quality on standard benchmarks.", abstractCn: "3D高斯溅射引入各向异性3D高斯作为直接辐射场表示，避免了NeRF所需的高代价光线步进。它采用基于瓦片的可微光栅化管线，配合GPU友好的alpha合成实现高效的新视角合成。自适应密度控制在训练过程中分裂和修剪高斯，逐步优化场景几何。该方法在标准基准上实现了超过100 FPS的实时渲染，同时视觉质量匹配或超越NeRF。" },
